{"op": "set-kind", "entity": {"id": "a4ff642f-28f8-416b-9ee3-338909612357", "name": "PUBLIX SUPER MARKETS, INC."}, "kind": "organization", "date": "2026-09-04", "note": "The Publix corporation, not a committee. It never registered (no committee_registrations row, files nothing) and appears only as a contributor in recipients' reports — $13.65M of corporate checks to committees — and as a payee in candidates' expenditure reports (grocery purchases). Kinded 'committee', the trace walked through it as a conduit and attributed its corporate giving pro-rata to whoever had bought groceries there: a candidate who spent $603 was credited with $13,699. As an organization it is an origin, which is what corporate treasury money is. The dormant CCE 'Publix People for Good Government' (0 rows; CCEs were abolished in 2013) is the old PAC; Publix now gives corporate funds directly."}
